{"id": "OR-002-extended-connect-protocol", "axis": "pseudo-header-acceptance", "input": ":protocol on a non-CONNECT request that also has :method, :path, and :scheme", "verdicts": {"h1": "n/a:no-pseudo-headers", "h2": "reject:ProtocolRequiresConnect", "h3": "accept:default-switch-false-skips-must-be-CONNECT", "yarp": "UNKNOWN:no-committed-C6-snippet"}, "divergence": "H1 reconstructs method, target, and version from the request line and has no :protocol slot. H2 aborts a non-CONNECT request that carries :protocol. H3 recognizes :protocol, stores it, and runs the must-be-CONNECT check only when EnableWebTransportAndH3Datagrams is true. That getter is an AppContext switch; TryGetSwitch failing leaves it false, so the default path does not throw for this field-set. Reset forces IsExtendedConnectRequest false, and the H3 10.0.13 decompilation contains no assignment of that flag to true. ClearPseudoRequestHeaders then drops the protocol bit from the enumerated header set. H3 accepts a field H1 cannot carry and H2 rejects. The field is removed from enumeration before a downstream would see ordinary headers. YARP is UNKNOWN.", "evidence": {"h1": "evidence/c5/Http1Connection.decompiled.cs:277-309 | C5:c5-kestrel/decomp/after/Microsoft.AspNetCore.Server.Kestrel.Core.Internal.Http.Http1Connection.decompiled.cs:277-309", "h2": "evidence/c7/Http2Stream.decompiled.cs:265-288 | C7@434e35b:c7-kestrel-h3/decomp/h2/10.0.13/Microsoft.AspNetCore.Server.Kestrel.Core.Internal.Http2.Http2Stream.decompiled.cs:265-288", "h3": "evidence/c7/Http3Stream.decompiled.cs:115 | C7@434e35b:c7-kestrel-h3/decomp/h3/10.0.13/Microsoft.AspNetCore.Server.Kestrel.Core.Internal.Http3.Http3Stream.decompiled.cs:115 ;; evidence/c7/Http3Stream.decompiled.cs:533-563 | C7@434e35b:c7-kestrel-h3/decomp/h3/10.0.13/Microsoft.AspNetCore.Server.Kestrel.Core.Internal.Http3.Http3Stream.decompiled.cs:533-563 ;; evidence/c7/Http3Stream.decompiled.cs:464-492 | C7@434e35b:c7-kestrel-h3/decomp/h3/10.0.13/Microsoft.AspNetCore.