{"id": "OR-008-te-token-not-trailers", "axis": "header-acceptance", "input": "literal header te whose value is not the bytes trailers", "verdicts": {"h1": "accept:stored-as-TE", "h2": "reject:literal-te-unless-trailers", "h3": "reject:literal-te-unless-trailers", "yarp": "UNKNOWN:no-committed-C6-snippet"}, "divergence": "H1 Append matches the two-byte name te and stores it on the TE field. That is not HasTransferEncoding, so it does not select the chunked body. H3 and H2 literal validation treat the name te as connection-specific unless the value bytes equal trailers, and then throw. H3 has no static-table te entry, and the QPACK dynamic table is not live, so the literal path is the H3 path. This is accept-versus-reject of a header. An H3 front throws before any forward. No committed forwarder shows the header crossing to another hop. YARP is UNKNOWN.", "evidence": {"h1": "evidence/c5/HttpRequestHeaders.decompiled.cs:7617-7623 | C5:c5-kestrel/decomp/after/Microsoft.AspNetCore.Server.Kestrel.Core.Internal.Http.HttpRequestHeaders.decompiled.cs:7617-7623 ;; evidence/c5/HttpRequestHeaders.decompiled.cs:449 | C5:c5-kestrel/decomp/after/Microsoft.AspNetCore.Server.Kestrel.Core.Internal.Http.HttpRequestHeaders.decompiled.cs:449 ;; evidence/c5/HttpRequestHeaders.decompiled.cs:7986-7994 | C5:c5-kestrel/decomp/after/Microsoft.AspNetCore.Server.Kestrel.Core.Internal.Http.HttpRequestHeaders.decompiled.cs:7986-7994", "h2": "evidence/c7/Http2Connection.decompiled.cs:171-173 | C7@434e35b:c7-kestrel-h3/decomp/h2/10.0.13/Microsoft.AspNetCore.Server.Kestrel.Core.Internal.Http2.Http2Connection.decompiled.cs:171-173 ;; evidence/c7/Http2Connection.decompiled.cs:1228-1231 | C7@434e35b:c7-kestrel-h3/decomp/h2/10.0.13/Microsoft.AspNetCore.Server.Kestrel.Core.Internal.Http2.Http2Connection.decompiled.cs:1228-1231 ;; evidence/c7/Http2Connection.decompiled.cs:1364-1374 | C7@434e35b:c7-kestrel-h3/decomp/h2/10.0.13/Microsoft.AspNetCore.Server.Kestrel.Core.Internal.Http2.Http2Connection.decompil